# Practical 01 - Installation of Angular

## Aim
To install and configure Angular on Windows and Ubuntu operating systems.


# Part A: Angular Installation on Windows

## Requirements
- Windows 10/11
- Node.js
- npm
- Angular CLI
- Visual Studio Code

## Step 1: Install Node.js

Download and install Node.js from the official website.

After installation, open Command Prompt or PowerShell and check:

node -v

## Step 2: Check npm

Run:

npm -v

## Step 3: Install Angular CLI

Run:

npm install -g @angular/cli

## Step 4: Check Angular Installation

Run:

ng version

## Step 5: Create Angular Project

Run:

ng new my-angular-app

## Step 6: Open the Project

Run:

cd my-angular-app

## Step 7: Run the Angular Application

Run:

ng serve --open

## Result

Angular was successfully installed on Windows and the Angular application was successfully executed.

