# Part B: Angular Installation on Ubuntu

## Requirements
- Ubuntu Linux
- Node.js
- npm
- Angular CLI
- Visual Studio Code

## Step 1: Update Ubuntu

Open Terminal and run:

sudo apt update

## Step 2: Install Node.js and npm

Run:

sudo apt install nodejs npm

## Step 3: Check Node.js

Run:

node -v

## Step 4: Check npm

Run:

npm -v

## Step 5: Install Angular CLI

Run:

sudo npm install -g @angular/cli

## Step 6: Check Angular Installation

Run:

ng version

## Step 7: Create Angular Project

Run:

ng new my-angular-app

## Step 8: Open the Project

Run:

cd my-angular-app

## Step 9: Run the Angular Application

Run:

ng serve --open

## Result

Angular was successfully installed on Ubuntu and the Angular application was successfully executed.
